<title>UK: Algeria ups Sept LPG prices by $15-$25/tonne-trade.</title>
<headline>Algeria ups Sept LPG prices by $15-$25/tonne-trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state oil company Sonatrach raised its September liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) prices by $15-$25 per tonne, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>Propane was hiked by $25 to $190.00 per tonne and butane was raised by $15 to $195.00, both fob Bedhioua.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
